{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795190000000-reviewer-p1d-agyflash.gemini-3.8-flash.findings.md /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795190000000-reviewer-p1d-agyflash.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-20 16:05:22 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-20 23:05:22 ICT\nCoding-Agent: agy\nSession-ID: eb1f719e-2fac-476b-9a8e-735295f3f52e\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-20 16:05:22 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-20 23:05:22 ICT (+07)  \nSession-ID: eb1f719e-2fac-476b-9a8e-735295f3f52e  \nReviewer: Gemini 3.8 Flash (High)  \nTask: Review P1d — uniform yin.repl launcher (commit `43b1da29` on `feat/p1d-uniform-launcher`)  \nTarget: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher  \n\n---\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nCommit `43b1da29` implements the uniform launcher entry point `bb yin-repl --backend <jvm|node|dart|jolt-chez|jolt-gambit>` through [src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj) and extends [src/dev/jolt_launch.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/jolt_launch.clj). The Lane B child command construction remains byte-identical for existing tasks. Gambit interactive terminal passthrough is verified over a genuine slave PTY, and boot caching correctly tracks compiler and source hashes without stale-boot risk for dynamic Yin Clojure code.\n\nHowever, the commit introduces **two out-of-scope production changes**, one of which inappropriately pollutes production entry points with test/launcher harness protocols, and suffers from **unconditional build/bootstrap triggers** on `dart`, `node`, and `jolt-gambit` that severely degrade launch performance.\n\nRecommendation: **ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES**.\n\n---\n\n### Gates Re-run & Outcomes\n\nAll gates were re-executed locally from the worktree with explicit timeouts:\n\n| Gate / Command | Outcome | Details / Observed Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bb bootstrap:jolt` | **PASS** | Exit 0; `jolt f22df3c7... with 7 submodules verified`; `jolt smoke (+ 1 2) => 3`. |\n| `bb smoke:jolt` | **PASS** | Exit 0; 6 `PASS` lines; `SUMMARY ok`. |\n| `bb smoke:jolt-target` (`--target chez`) | **PASS** | Exit 0; `VERDICT target chez identity \"jolt-target: chez\" child answered 3: ok`. |\n| `bb smoke:jolt-target --target gambit` | **PASS** | Exit 0; `VERDICT target gambit identity \"jolt-target: gambit\" child answered 3: ok`. |\n| `bb yin-repl --backend jvm` | **PASS** | Exit 0; `yin-backend: jvm` -> `yin> 3` -> `Bye`. |\n| `bb yin-repl --backend node` | **PASS** | Exit 0; `yin-backend: node` -> `yin> 3` -> `Bye`. |\n| `bb yin-repl --backend dart` | **CONDITIONAL PASS** | Direct binary `./build/yin-repl-peer` exits 0 with `yin-backend: dart` -> `yin> 3` -> `Bye`. Invocation via `bb yin-repl --backend dart` fails under standard sandbox mode due to unconditional rebuild triggering Flutter's write to `~/.config/flutter`. |\n| `bb yin-repl --backend jolt-chez` | **PASS** | Exit 0; `jolt-target: chez` -> `Host: jolt gambit-ffi-p1c-f22df3c7 / Chez 10.4.1` -> `yin> 3` -> `Bye`. |\n| `bb yin-repl --backend jolt-gambit` | **PASS (startup)** | Emits `jolt-target: gambit`, validates identity gate, outputs capability notice; loads namespaces in interpreted Scheme. |\n| `bb yin-repl --help` | **PASS** | Exit 0; surfaces all 5 backends, capability limits, and `-- --help` forwarding. |\n\n---\n\n### Priority Findings & Analysis\n\n#### P1: Scope & Production Changes (Accept/Reject Hinge)\n\n1. **`src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt`** ([driver.jolt#L22-L23](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt#L22-L23), [driver.jolt#L72](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt#L72), [driver.jolt#L152](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt#L152)):\n   - **Origin**: Upstream Jolt commit `e20e2174bf4661dcb7b721437ff2847c25de429d` (*\"Register poller waits directly with the kernel\"*) removed `(ffi/defcfn c-read \"read\" ...)` and `c-pipe` from `stdlib/jolt/io_poller.clj`. Consequently, `dao.stream.waitset.driver` on master crashed at runtime with `No such var: poller/c-read`.\n   - **Judgement (a)**: Necessary for the goal. Without this change, Chez `yin.repl` cannot run on the pinned Jolt fork.\n   - **Judgement (b)**: Strictly **behavior-preserving**. `driver.jolt` already loads libc via `(ffi/load-library)` and `c-pipe`. Binding `c-read` directly with `[:int :pointer :size_t] :ssize_t` restores the exact POSIX `read(2)` binding previously imported from `poller`.\n   - **Judgement (c)**: Must be retained, but should be separated into its own upstream-compatibility fix commit rather than hidden inside the launcher feature PR.\n\n2. **`src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc`** ([main.cljc#L69-L81](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc#L69-L81), [main.cljc#L90](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc#L90), [main.cljc#L98](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc#L98), [main.cljc#L106](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc#L106)):\n   - **Origin**: Added `report-launcher!` to emit `yin-backend: jvm`, `yin-backend: node`, and `jolt-target: chez` when `DATOMWORLD_YIN_LAUNCHER=1`.\n   - **Judgement (a)**: **Bends production unnecessarily**. The task brief explicitly restricted identity line reporting to Jolt backends: *\"and every child prints the Lane B identity line (`jolt-target: <t>` for the jolt backends) with the driver asserting it\"*. The author generalized this by inventing `yin-backend:` and injecting environment checks into production `-main` entry points across `:clj`, `:jolt`, and `:cljs`.\n   - **Judgement (c)**: **Revert**. Production Yin shell code must remain clean of test harness / launcher multiplexing markers. Jolt Chez identity can be confirmed without altering production source (e.g. via standard target invocation or wrapper `-e` probe).\n\n#### P2: Zero-Change Rule\n- **Diff against master**: Byte-identical command strings confirmed.\n  - [src/dev/jolt_launch.clj#L82-L107](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/jolt_launch.clj#L82-L107): `launch-command` refactored prefix assembly into `toolchain-command` and added optional `:cd?`. When `:cd?` is false (default for all existing callers), the resulting string matches master byte-for-byte:\n    `\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && export JOLT_TARGET=chez && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt\" alias script \"\\\"$@\\\"\"`\n  - [bb.edn#L258-L263](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/bb.edn#L258-L263): The commit purely appends `yin-repl`. Existing tasks are untouched.\n  - `:jvm` invocation in `yin_repl_launch.clj` uses `[\"clj\" \"-M:clj-yin-repl\"]`, matching canonical documentation in [README.md#L114](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/README.md#L114).\n\n#### P3: Gambit Interactive Passthrough & PTY\n- **Verification method**: The author used an isolated tmux session where `lsof` confirmed `gsi` had both fd 0 and fd 1 attached to `/dev/ttys010`.\n- **The \"42\" expression**: Not part of any fixture or corpus. The author submitted `(+ 19 23)` -> `42` to verify that dynamic evaluation operated over the interactive terminal stream rather than replaying static responses.\n- **PTY vs. Pipe**: In [src/dev/jolt_launch.clj#L147-L149](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/jolt_launch.clj#L147-L149), `run-terminal-child` invokes `babashka.process/process` with `{:in :inherit :out :inherit :err :stream}`. In a terminal or tmux session, fd 0 and fd 1 are inherited directly from the caller's TTY (genuine terminal attach).\n- **Identity assertion on interactive path**: Confirmed. `run-terminal-child` reads lines from stderr until `identity-prefix` is observed and evaluated with `assert-identity!`. Only after validation does it copy subsequent stderr to `System/err`.\n\n#### P4: Boot Caching & Stale-Boot Risk\n- **Hashing**: [build-yin-boot.py#L58-L64](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/build/p1d-tools/jolt/host/gambit/build-yin-boot.py#L58-L64) hashes `build-yin-boot.py`, `gsc`, and recursively all `(##include ...)` sources starting from `BOOT`. Staged compilation occurs under an `flock` and moves atomically into `build/gambit-yin/`.\n- **Runtime bridge**: [yin_repl_launch.clj#L82-L111](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L82-L111) snapshots Makefile, `host/gambit/ffi`, and compiler toolchain inputs via `build-cache`.\n- **Stale-boot risk**: **Zero risk for Clojure Yin code**. The compiled boot artifact is purely the underlying Scheme runtime (`boot.ss`). Yin Clojure namespaces are interpreted dynamically from `$DATOMWORLD_ROOT` at runtime by `yin-repl-native.ss`. Clojure source edits take effect immediately without requiring boot recompilation.\n\n#### P5: Capability Notes\n- [src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L12-L30](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L12-L30):\n  - `--help` explicitly documents:\n    - `Local --index-store mem session; no :yang/python frontend or WebSocket serving.`\n    - `Blocking FFI refuses inline: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target.`\n  - `jolt-gambit` startup prints both capability notices to stderr immediately.\n  - Honestly and accurately surfaced.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Findings (P1 - P3)\n\n- **[P1] Production coupling in `test/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc`** ([slice_peer.cljc#L365-L371](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/test/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc#L365-L371)):\n  The author altered `peer-main` to inspect `DATOMWORLD_YIN_LAUNCHER` and delegate to `shell/-main`. While this satisfied the brief's instruction to execute `build/yin-repl-peer`, it overloads a test harness peer with interactive shell routing based on an environment variable.\n- **[P2] Unconditional prerequisite re-execution** ([yin_repl_launch.clj#L126](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L126), [yin_repl_launch.clj#L172](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L172), [yin_repl_launch.clj#L174](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj#L174)):\n  - `gambit-session` runs `(task! \"bootstrap:jolt\")` unconditionally on every launch (unlike line 176 for `jolt-chez`, which checks `fs/regular-file?`). This adds 5+ seconds of submodule and toolchain checks to every gambit REPL invocation.\n  - Line 174 runs `(task! \"build:yin-repl-peer\")` unconditionally on every Dart launch, triggering a full ~15-second Flutter/Dart compile even when `build/yin-repl-peer` already exists.\n  - Line 172 runs `(task! \"build:yin-repl-node\")` unconditionally on every Node launch.\n  - **Remedy**: Gate these behind target presence checks (`when-not (fs/regular-file? ...)`).\n\n---\n\n### Final Recommendation\n\n**ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES**\n\n#### Required Fixes Before Landing:\n1. **Revert changes to `src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc`**: Strip `report-launcher!` and remove `DATOMWORLD_YIN_LAUNCHER` logic from shipped production entry points. The brief does not require JVM or Node to report `yin-backend:`.\n2. **Split `src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt` into a separate commit**: The `c-read` fix is valid, correct, and required for Jolt Chez, but belongs in a distinct bugfix commit citing Jolt upstream commit `e20e2174`.\n3. **Guard prerequisite builds in `src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj`**:\n   - Line 126 (`jolt-gambit`): Check `(when-not (fs/regular-file? \"build/tools/jolt-env.sh\") (task! \"bootstrap:jolt\"))`.\n   - Line 172 (`node`): Check `(when-not (fs/regular-file? \"target/yin-repl.js\") (task! \"build:yin-repl-node\"))`.\n   - Line 174 (`dart`): Check `(when-not (fs/regular-file? \"build/yin-repl-peer\") (task! \"build:yin-repl-peer\"))`.\n\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-20 15:52:18 GMT\nSession-ID: pending (capture conversation_id)\n# Task: review P1d — the uniform yin.repl launcher (43b1da29 on feat/p1d-uniform-launcher)\n\nRole: Review (adversarial; author codex gpt-6.2-sol — Gemini family independent)\nImplementers:\n- Model: gemini-3.8-flash-high | Assigned: see Created-Local | Status: active\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/p1d-uniform-launcher,\n  branch feat/p1d-uniform-launcher, commit 43b1da29 (base = current master).\n- Brief: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795187823308-engineer-p1d-uniform-launcher.prompt.md\n- Author findings: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795187823308-engineer-p1d-uniform-launcher.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\n\n## Review priorities\n\nP1 SCOPE + PRODUCTION CHANGES (the orchestrator's flag): the commit touches\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc (+18) and src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt\n(POSIX read binding — author rationale: \"compatibility with the pinned Jolt\nversion\") — both OUTSIDE the brief's owned set (bb.edn tasks + the src/dev\nseam). Judge: (a) is each change necessary for the goal, or does it bend\nproduction to make a smoke pass? (b) is the waitset change behavior-preserving\nfor the EXISTING Chez lane (diff it against master and reason about the\nruntime effect), or does it alter semantics? (c) should these be split out/\nreverted with the launcher adapted instead? This is the accept/reject hinge.\nP2 Zero-change rule: diff the default :jvm path and the existing bb tasks'\nchild command construction against master — byte-identical?\nP3 The gambit interactive passthrough: how was the tmux PTY check verified\n(作者 claims 3 and 42 returned — what is 42 in the corpus?); is the stdin\nattach real (TTY) or a pipe approximation; does the identity gate still assert\non the interactive path?\nP4 Boot caching: build/gambit-yin digest stamp — rebuild-on-change correct?\nstale-boot risk?\nP5 Capability notes: does --help surface the jolt-gambit degradation honestly?\n\nYou may run: the five backend smokes (bb yin-repl --backend ... with one-line\ninputs), bb smoke:jolt, bb smoke:jolt-target, bb bootstrap:jolt, git diff —\nforeground, explicit timeouts, writes confined to the worktree's build/.\nNo suite lanes. READ-ONLY on sources: do not modify or commit anything.\n\nDeliverable: findings as your final response beginning with Completed-*\nheader fields; findings P0-P3 with file:line; gates re-run with outcomes;\nclosing RECOMMENDATION: ACCEPT / ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES (list) / REJECT (reasons).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
